WEBVTT

00:06.840 --> 00:08.512
Wanna hear a great band?

00:10.240 --> 00:13.312
- Sure.
- They're called Bucket of Hate.

00:26.720 --> 00:27.948
What do you think?

00:28.680 --> 00:32.389
Nice beat.

00:33.480 --> 00:35.072
Oh, my goodness.

00:35.240 --> 00:36.673
Quite a mouth on this fella.

00:38.040 --> 00:41.237
I guess that's why they're not called
Bucket of Bunnies, huh?

00:42.240 --> 00:44.037
- Who's he listening to?
- Bucket of Hate.

00:44.200 --> 00:45.952
They're good.
Reminds me of early Who.

00:46.120 --> 00:47.314
- Who? What?
- Yeah.

00:47.480 --> 00:49.311
- The band's called Who.
- Bucket of Hate.

00:53.080 --> 00:55.230
And I work for your family.

00:57.560 --> 01:01.439
Boy, I never knew there were
so many rhymes for suicide.

01:01.600 --> 01:03.079
Yeah, what's patricide?

01:04.360 --> 01:07.079
It means to honor thy father.

01:07.880 --> 01:09.791
Oh, well, then that song
doesn't make sense.

01:10.160 --> 01:13.869
Yeah, well, I'm still trying to figure out
what a su-su-sudio is.

01:15.240 --> 01:17.993
So BOH is playing
at the Santa Monica Civic Center...

01:18.160 --> 01:19.195
...next weekend.

01:19.560 --> 01:20.675
Cool.

01:20.840 --> 01:22.876
My friend Seth Friedman got tickets.
Can I go?

01:23.040 --> 01:24.837
- How are you gonna get there?
- Car.

01:27.480 --> 01:28.469
Thank you.

01:30.120 --> 01:31.553
- Whose car?
- Seth's brother.

01:31.720 --> 01:34.518
He's 17, and he's never been
in an accident that was his fault.

01:38.120 --> 01:39.189
I don't think so.

01:39.360 --> 01:40.509
Why not?

01:40.680 --> 01:44.468
Why don't I think it's appropriate for a
13-year-old to go with no supervision?

01:44.640 --> 01:46.392
I told you. Rocco is 17.

01:47.040 --> 01:49.156
- His name is Rocco?
- Yeah.

01:49.320 --> 01:52.676
So Rocco Friedman?

01:53.160 --> 01:54.593
Yeah. Do you know him?

01:54.760 --> 01:57.638
No, but I'm not letting someone
named Rocco Friedman drive you...

01:57.800 --> 01:59.791
...to a Bucket of Hate concert.

02:00.200 --> 02:01.599
That's it. Just no?

02:01.760 --> 02:02.829
Oh, I'm sorry.

02:03.000 --> 02:04.831
No way in hell.

02:05.440 --> 02:06.793
Oh, man.

02:07.320 --> 02:10.073
- What's going on?
- My dad sucks.

02:11.480 --> 02:15.359
You know, in certain primitive cultures,
when a boy hits puberty...

02:15.520 --> 02:18.159
...they tie him to a big rock,
and throw him in the ocean.

02:18.320 --> 02:19.799
- No, they don't.
- Okay.

02:19.960 --> 02:21.996
But you can't argue with the logic.

02:22.280 --> 02:23.554
No, I can't.

02:23.720 --> 02:25.711
Here. Your girlfriend's in the paper.

02:25.880 --> 02:27.359
Really? What for?

02:27.520 --> 02:31.195
She's being honored by the Southern
California Trial Lawyers Association.

02:33.200 --> 02:34.758
"Judge of the Year."

02:34.920 --> 02:38.435
Yeah, I guess it's time to get out
the old tux for the banquet, huh?

02:38.600 --> 02:40.033
What banquet?

02:40.200 --> 02:42.350
The one at the Beverly Hilton
next Saturday.

02:43.000 --> 02:45.389
Oh, right.

02:46.000 --> 02:48.150
Yeah, I don't think I'm going to that.

02:48.520 --> 02:49.953
Why not?

02:50.120 --> 02:52.680
You know,
I hate the whole dog and pony show.

02:52.840 --> 02:54.831
Getting dressed up,
speeches, rubber chicken...

02:55.000 --> 02:57.594
- She didn't invite you, did she?
- Didn't even mention it.

03:00.600 --> 03:02.352
That's gotta sting.

03:04.560 --> 03:05.788
You know, I agree with Jake.

03:05.960 --> 03:07.029
You do suck.

03:36.720 --> 03:40.508
God, Charlie, you are great.

03:41.320 --> 03:42.639
No.

03:42.800 --> 03:44.119
I'm serious.

03:44.280 --> 03:47.477
You are the best lover I have ever had.

03:47.640 --> 03:50.712
It's probably just the flawless
technique and the big penis.

03:52.840 --> 03:54.910
Probably.

03:55.480 --> 03:56.959
I was wondering.

03:57.120 --> 04:00.476
- You got any plans next Saturday?
- Next Saturday?

04:01.400 --> 04:03.197
Oh, as a matter of fact, I do.

04:04.400 --> 04:05.719
What might they be?

04:05.880 --> 04:07.472
The plans?

04:07.640 --> 04:09.710
Just some business thing. Very boring.

04:09.880 --> 04:11.950
- Business.
- Yeah, business.

04:12.120 --> 04:14.759
Might this be
the business we're speaking of?

04:16.000 --> 04:17.513
"Dilbert"?

04:19.400 --> 04:20.958
This?

04:21.120 --> 04:22.109
Oh, that.

04:22.280 --> 04:23.679
Oh, I can explain.

04:23.840 --> 04:25.478
I would love an explanation.

04:25.640 --> 04:28.393
Well, I just thought
it wouldn't be your kind of thing.

04:28.560 --> 04:31.199
You know, it's just judges,
lawyers, local politicians.

04:31.360 --> 04:33.749
- Are you going with somebody else?
- No.

04:33.920 --> 04:36.593
So you'd rather go alone than take me?

04:37.360 --> 04:38.713
I know it seems that way.

04:40.040 --> 04:42.679
- You're ashamed of me, aren't you?
- Oh, no, Charlie.

04:42.840 --> 04:46.719
Sure, you can use me for sex, but
God forbid we're out in public together.

04:46.880 --> 04:47.949
That is not true.

04:48.120 --> 04:49.109
And let me remind you.

04:49.280 --> 04:50.952
It's the best sex you've ever had.

04:51.120 --> 04:53.759
- Charlie...
- Your words, not mine.

04:53.920 --> 04:57.435
Look, the last thing in the world
I wanna do is hurt your feelings.

04:57.600 --> 04:58.828
Well, you have.

05:03.040 --> 05:06.874
Would you like to go with me
to the banquet?

05:07.160 --> 05:09.594
No. I don't wanna go
where I'm not wanted.

05:10.000 --> 05:13.037
- What do you want me to do? Beg?
- A little, yeah.

05:16.080 --> 05:18.548
Please come with me to the banquet.

05:20.400 --> 05:21.992
A little more.

05:22.960 --> 05:25.428
Pretty please?

05:26.040 --> 05:27.951
Come with me.

05:29.320 --> 05:30.469
All right.

05:31.960 --> 05:34.713
But then we gotta talk
about this banquet thing.

05:40.040 --> 05:42.873
Jake, do you want Grandmommy
to teach you how to use chopsticks?

05:43.040 --> 05:45.838
Don't confuse him.
He just learned how to use a fork.

05:47.840 --> 05:49.159
Real funny, Alan.

05:53.560 --> 05:55.039
Alan? What happened to Dad?

05:55.200 --> 05:57.111
He turned into Benito Mussoroni.

06:00.000 --> 06:01.274
The San Francisco treat?

06:03.440 --> 06:05.954
It's Mussolini, professor.

06:06.120 --> 06:08.156
He's upset, I won't let him
go to a concert.

06:08.320 --> 06:11.039
- Why not?
- Because there's no adult supervision.

06:11.200 --> 06:13.077
Oh, don't be such a fuddy-duddy, Alan.

06:13.240 --> 06:16.152
He's a teenager. Teenagers don't go
to concerts with their parents.

06:16.320 --> 06:18.311
I'm with Evelyn on this.

06:20.000 --> 06:21.956
Forget it.
You are not going to the concert.

06:22.120 --> 06:23.109
Oh, listen to you.

06:23.280 --> 06:26.078
Remember I said you couldn't go
to that Peter Frampton concert?

06:26.240 --> 06:28.435
You snuck out of the house
and went anyway.

06:28.600 --> 06:30.272
- Really?
- Mom, no.

06:31.000 --> 06:34.629
I was in Martinique at the time,
but the housekeeper was beside herself.

06:36.600 --> 06:39.398
And I was severely punished
for that, right?

06:39.560 --> 06:42.791
Oh, sure, I tried grounding you,
and taking away TV privileges.

06:42.960 --> 06:46.316
But at a certain point, every parent
has to accept that they're powerless...

06:46.480 --> 06:48.357
...when it comes
to controlling a teenager.

06:48.520 --> 06:49.669
- Really?
- No.

06:49.840 --> 06:50.955
No, not really.

06:51.120 --> 06:53.031
Parents are powerful, very powerful.

06:56.000 --> 06:57.911
No, no:

06:59.200 --> 07:02.033
No, trust me.
I'm only doing this for your own good.

07:07.800 --> 07:08.789
What the hell was that?

07:09.560 --> 07:10.754
The same thing Grandma did.

07:10.920 --> 07:14.071
No, it's not. You sound
like you're coughing up a fur ball.

07:14.360 --> 07:16.635
Yeah, well, I'm making the same point.

07:20.960 --> 07:23.155
Did it even occur to you
that you could help me?

07:23.480 --> 07:26.233
I was not put on this Earth
to help you, Alan.

07:29.360 --> 07:30.634
You're my mother.

07:30.800 --> 07:34.110
Yes, and as you never tire
of pointing out, not a good one.

07:35.840 --> 07:37.512
Hey, Alan, do we have
any snack bars?

07:37.880 --> 07:39.154
Right-hand cabinet. Why?

07:39.520 --> 07:41.431
Oh, I need something
to soak up the booze...

07:41.600 --> 07:44.319
...I'll have to drink
to make it through this dinner.

07:44.640 --> 07:45.629
What's the occasion?

07:46.200 --> 07:48.156
My girlfriend is being honored
at a banquet.

07:48.320 --> 07:51.073
Oh, I thought the Adult Film Awards
were in Vegas.

07:53.440 --> 07:54.953
She happens to be a judge.

07:55.120 --> 07:57.031
Of the Adult Film Awards?

07:58.000 --> 07:59.149
No. No.

07:59.320 --> 08:01.880
A judge
in the Los Angeles Municipal Court.

08:02.040 --> 08:03.439
So do I look okay?

08:03.800 --> 08:05.392
It's a tuxedo. You can't go wrong.

08:05.560 --> 08:07.869
I wanna fit in.
This is a very conservative crowd.

08:08.960 --> 08:10.757
Well, then you can go wrong.

08:10.920 --> 08:12.194
Thanks. Like I'm not nervous?

08:12.360 --> 08:16.353
Oh, sweetheart, if you're nervous,
just try one of these. It'll relax you.

08:16.520 --> 08:18.158
Oh, perfect.

08:18.320 --> 08:21.517
Charlie, you just can't pop a pill
without knowing what it is.

08:21.680 --> 08:24.114
She just said what it is.
Thanks, Mom, gotta go.

08:24.280 --> 08:27.352
Bye, sweetheart. Have a
good time with your judge, darling.

08:28.160 --> 08:29.479
That will last.

08:30.880 --> 08:33.235
I don't know.
I think he's really trying on this one.

08:38.960 --> 08:40.029
What?

08:40.920 --> 08:42.148
Nothing.

08:43.640 --> 08:47.918
Guess I'll just have to watch my DVD
of &lt;i>Fantasia&lt;/i> on the natch tonight.

08:54.320 --> 08:55.594
Congratulations, Your Honor.

08:55.960 --> 08:57.951
- Well deserved.
- Oh, thank you, councilman.

08:58.120 --> 09:00.156
I'd like you to meet my friend
Charlie Harper.

09:00.320 --> 09:02.880
Charlie, this is Councilman Stewart.

09:05.960 --> 09:08.952
- Charlie?
- Yeah, hi. How are you?

09:09.360 --> 09:11.191
Again, congratulations.

09:12.120 --> 09:13.633
Thanks.

09:15.320 --> 09:17.550
Charlie, are you okay?

09:18.280 --> 09:19.679
I'm wonderful.

09:21.520 --> 09:23.954
Look at all the colors.

09:24.680 --> 09:28.070
It's like I'm drinking a rainbow.

09:39.240 --> 09:40.992
Hang on. He's probably in his room.

09:41.160 --> 09:43.549
Jake, your mom's on the phone.

09:45.360 --> 09:46.713
Jake?

09:51.520 --> 09:52.794
Jake?

10:00.280 --> 10:02.874
Son of a bitch.

10:03.040 --> 10:05.873
- &lt;i>Alan, what's going on? Are you all right?&lt;/i>
- What?

10:06.040 --> 10:08.952
Oh, I stubbed my toe.

10:09.240 --> 10:12.755
Yeah, yeah. It may be broken.

10:13.800 --> 10:17.554
Yeah, I'm gonna go
to the emergency room.

10:17.720 --> 10:20.314
Oh, no, no, I have to take
Jake with me...

10:20.480 --> 10:24.268
...so we can go in the carpool lane.

10:24.440 --> 10:26.351
Jake, help Daddy find his toenail.

10:26.520 --> 10:29.080
I'll have him call you later, okay?

10:29.240 --> 10:31.595
Son of a bitch.

10:35.800 --> 10:39.509
So without further ado,
here's our guest of honor...

10:39.680 --> 10:43.514
...Judge of the Year,
and I'm proud to say my good friend...

10:43.680 --> 10:45.477
...Judge Linda Harris.
- Yeah.

10:45.640 --> 10:47.278
Yeah.

10:51.640 --> 10:53.995
Who the judge? You the judge.

10:56.760 --> 10:58.352
I'm hitting that.

11:22.320 --> 11:25.392
Los Angeles, thank you.

11:28.560 --> 11:30.949
Hey, look who's here.

11:31.120 --> 11:32.155
Keep it down.

11:32.320 --> 11:35.039
Right, we don't wanna wake me.

11:36.480 --> 11:38.072
What are you doing sitting out here?

11:38.240 --> 11:40.037
I can't stand up.

11:40.480 --> 11:42.357
Don't make a thing out of it.

11:43.760 --> 11:44.795
What are you doing?

11:44.960 --> 11:46.632
I snuck out to see a concert.

11:47.440 --> 11:49.112
No way.

11:49.880 --> 11:52.633
That is so cool.

11:56.160 --> 11:57.479
Okay.

11:57.640 --> 11:59.471
Third time's the charm.

12:00.240 --> 12:02.959
Hey, wanna know what else is cool?

12:03.120 --> 12:04.951
Check this out.

12:08.120 --> 12:10.395
Hey, hey, I'm caroling here.

12:10.560 --> 12:12.676
You should be bringing me Cocoa
and Gingerbread.

12:13.040 --> 12:14.314
Cocoa and gingerbread?

12:14.480 --> 12:15.469
Yeah.

12:15.640 --> 12:17.312
They work at the Spearmint Rhino.

12:19.560 --> 12:22.632
But I digress.

12:23.520 --> 12:25.670
- Where were we?
- My dad doesn't know I went out.

12:25.840 --> 12:27.831
So now I have to sneak back in.

12:28.400 --> 12:31.551
Well, then you certainly
don't wanna go through this door.

12:32.200 --> 12:33.918
- Why not?
- Why not?

12:34.080 --> 12:35.229
I'll tell you why not.

12:42.800 --> 12:45.314
- What?
- Why not?

12:45.760 --> 12:47.352
Why not what?

12:47.720 --> 12:49.278
Why can't I go through that door?

12:50.000 --> 12:52.230
Oh, well, why didn't you say so?

12:53.920 --> 12:57.674
If I know your dad, and sadly I do...

12:58.000 --> 13:01.675
...he's sitting in there right now,
just waiting to tie you to a rock...

13:01.840 --> 13:04.195
...and throw you in the ocean.

13:04.880 --> 13:05.915
What?

13:06.320 --> 13:09.710
Sorry.
I may have put the idea in his head.

13:11.280 --> 13:12.952
Follow me.

13:13.680 --> 13:16.717
- Where are we going?
- Hey, I'll ask the questions.

13:18.600 --> 13:20.272
Where are we going?

13:24.640 --> 13:25.959
All right.

13:27.120 --> 13:28.712
I'm okay.

13:31.440 --> 13:33.032
Here, grab my... What do you call it?

13:33.200 --> 13:34.519
- Hand.

13:36.200 --> 13:37.952
I'm okay.

13:38.400 --> 13:41.198
That's great.
But you're sitting on my head.

13:47.200 --> 13:49.430
Do you have any idea
how much trouble you're in?

13:49.600 --> 13:51.955
I do not.

13:52.520 --> 13:55.717
Do you have any idea
how beautiful you look in that light?

13:56.560 --> 14:00.314
- I'm not talking to you.
- Well, I'm not talking to you either.

14:00.480 --> 14:01.549
Except for right now.

14:01.720 --> 14:05.838
This is me talking to you,
but no longer.

14:07.200 --> 14:09.668
Would you please just go to sleep?

14:09.840 --> 14:10.875
Okey-dokey.

14:14.000 --> 14:18.516
- You and I have some talking to do.
- Will you make up your freaking mind?

14:25.360 --> 14:26.793
Morning.

14:29.040 --> 14:30.519
What? You're not talking to me?

14:30.880 --> 14:32.359
I looked up patricide.

14:35.960 --> 14:36.995
Really?

14:37.160 --> 14:38.752
When did you learn to spell?

14:39.880 --> 14:41.472
I sounded it out.

14:43.600 --> 14:44.919
Patricide, huh?

14:45.320 --> 14:47.072
Our little boy is growing up.

14:48.400 --> 14:50.118
He's just upset because he snuck out.

14:50.280 --> 14:51.838
So I grounded him for three months.

14:52.000 --> 14:54.355
- That ought to show him.
- What am I gonna do, Berta?

14:54.520 --> 14:56.556
- I can't hit him.
- Well, sure you can.

14:56.720 --> 14:59.439
You just gotta figure the wind,
and lead him.

15:01.280 --> 15:02.998
They're like pheasants.

15:03.520 --> 15:05.192
Very funny.

15:07.280 --> 15:08.838
What?

15:09.800 --> 15:11.597
Charlie's gonna wanna see this.

15:11.760 --> 15:13.876
No, he's not.

15:16.880 --> 15:18.598
Charlie, wake up.

15:18.760 --> 15:20.239
You need to see this.

15:20.400 --> 15:22.152
Can I throw up in it?

15:22.800 --> 15:26.031
- No.
- Then I don't need to see it.

15:26.200 --> 15:29.033
Charlie, do you remember
what you did last night?

15:32.680 --> 15:34.477
Oh, damn it.

15:35.000 --> 15:36.274
Did I get married?

15:38.280 --> 15:39.679
Hardly.

15:48.880 --> 15:53.556
Oh, you just know she's gonna
find a way to make this my fault.

15:59.240 --> 16:00.559
You climbed out the window?

16:00.720 --> 16:03.473
And got into a car
driven by a 17-year-old boy.

16:03.640 --> 16:07.599
It wasn't a car, Dad.
It was an extremely safe monster truck.

16:07.760 --> 16:10.797
I mean, even if Rocco hit another car,
he'd just crush it.

16:10.960 --> 16:13.076
The point is,
you disobeyed your father.

16:13.240 --> 16:15.390
That doesn't mean
I have to get grounded.

16:15.560 --> 16:17.790
In my opinion,
your punishment isn't severe enough.

16:17.960 --> 16:20.599
- Your mother's right.
- How come nobody asks my opinion?

16:20.760 --> 16:22.910
Go to your room.
I will talk to you later.

16:23.080 --> 16:24.559
Fine.

16:25.520 --> 16:27.909
Hey, thanks for backing me up here,
Judith.

16:28.080 --> 16:30.548
Now that he's a teenager,
we need to stick together to...

16:30.720 --> 16:32.836
You don't have a brain in your head,
do you?

16:33.000 --> 16:34.513
You have to watch teenagers, Alan.

16:34.680 --> 16:37.035
You can't just expect
they'll listen and obey.

16:37.200 --> 16:38.394
God, you're useless.

16:56.240 --> 16:58.071
Here. Let me give you a hand.

16:59.000 --> 17:00.991
- Really?
- Yeah.

17:01.160 --> 17:03.230
Now, come with me.

17:03.400 --> 17:05.834
- Where are we going?
- You're going back to your room.

17:06.000 --> 17:09.470
But I am going
to the sweet land of vindication.

17:09.840 --> 17:11.637
Oh, Judith.

17:17.400 --> 17:19.038
Yes?

17:19.760 --> 17:20.749
Hey.

17:20.920 --> 17:22.148
What are you doing here?

17:23.560 --> 17:25.516
I came to apologize.

17:25.680 --> 17:27.432
I am sorry about last night.

17:27.600 --> 17:31.673
You're sorry for ruining one of the most
important nights of my career?

17:31.840 --> 17:34.195
For embarrassing me
within an inch of my life?

17:34.360 --> 17:35.554
Well, yeah.

17:35.720 --> 17:37.312
I mean, unless I did something else.

17:38.480 --> 17:40.072
No, you did quite enough. Thank you.

17:40.520 --> 17:42.397
Look, I understand why you're mad.

17:42.560 --> 17:44.391
But it really wasn't my fault.

17:44.560 --> 17:46.994
I was nervous about last night,
so my mother gave me...

17:47.160 --> 17:49.196
...what I assumed
was one of her tranquilizers.

17:49.360 --> 17:51.271
Now I'm thinking it was
a little something...

17:51.440 --> 17:52.998
...she had left over
from Woodstock.

17:54.480 --> 17:59.429
Charlie, look,
you're a lot of fun and I like you.

17:59.920 --> 18:02.912
But people are talking about me
running for state senate next year.

18:03.080 --> 18:06.834
And I can't afford to be linked publicly
to someone like you.

18:07.000 --> 18:08.353
Well, that's not a problem.

18:08.520 --> 18:10.476
We'll just sneak around
and link privately.

18:10.880 --> 18:11.915
No, Charlie.

18:12.080 --> 18:14.753
Come on, all the guy politicians
have something on the side.

18:14.920 --> 18:16.433
Why shouldn't you?

18:22.080 --> 18:23.195
Take care.

18:28.360 --> 18:32.239
It would send a powerful message
to young women everywhere.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.433
- Bailiff.
- I'm going.

18:43.320 --> 18:45.197
Pretty flowers.

18:46.360 --> 18:48.078
Thanks.

18:48.640 --> 18:50.358
Wanna stick them in something?

18:56.880 --> 18:58.472
Never mind.

19:01.200 --> 19:02.872
I thought I was up to it, Alan.

19:03.040 --> 19:05.315
I thought I was ready
for a real relationship.

19:05.680 --> 19:08.069
That Linda and I would be a team.

19:08.240 --> 19:11.516
I'd stand by her as an accomplished
woman and a judge...

19:11.680 --> 19:14.035
...and she'd stand by me as a...

19:14.760 --> 19:16.432
Reformed whoremonger?

19:19.040 --> 19:21.190
- So you believe I was trying?
- I do.

19:21.360 --> 19:25.319
You know what? Someday, you'll look
back on this as a growing experience.

19:25.480 --> 19:27.471
Maybe. Someday.

19:29.440 --> 19:31.829
Oh, who could that be?

19:32.560 --> 19:34.312
- I ordered some takeout.
- Oh, nice.

19:34.480 --> 19:36.710
- Italian?
- Nope.

19:37.400 --> 19:38.958
Hi. Are you Charlie?

19:39.120 --> 19:40.997
Yeah. Come on in.

19:41.240 --> 19:42.719
Greek.

19:44.760 --> 19:45.988
Be patient with me.

19:46.160 --> 19:48.754
I'm coming off a bad breakup.

19:50.760 --> 19:54.878
And as usual,
Alan gets chicken pot pie.

20:19.840 --> 20:21.831
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

20:22.000 --> 20:23.991
